        "original_id": "40ef9384-e828-5bc9-ab2c-b7e4a59aa601",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Arrival, The Town\n- People: Denis Villeneuve, Eric Heisserer, Ted Chiang, Amy Adams, Jeremy Renner, Forest Whitaker, Dan Levine, Shawn Levy, Aaron Ryder, David Linde\n- Roles: director, writer, producer, actor, linguist\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor, Academy Award for Best Picture\n- Concepts: science fiction film, extraterrestrial communication\n\nFacts:\n- Ted Chiang wrote the 1998 short story \"Story of Your Life,\" which was the basis for the film Arrival.\n- Jeremy Renner was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for his performance in The Town (2010).\n- Arrival is a 2016 American science fiction film directed by Denis Villeneuve and written by Eric Heisserer.\n- Arrival stars Amy Adams, Jeremy Renner, and Forest Whitaker.\n- Arrival follows linguist Louise Banks, who is enlisted by the U.S. Army to translate communications from one of several extraterrestrial craft that have appeared around the world.\n- Dan Levine is best known for producing Arrival and received an Academy Award for Best Picture nomination for the film alongside Shawn Levy, Aaron Ryder, and David Linde.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
